# Party banter, act 3 (story/banter.gd): one exchange between two or three companions, played now and then on entering an area, once each. Every node opens
# with its act's gate and both speakers, so an exchange that can't be heard comes out empty and is skipped; any file named party_* plays anywhere.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ act3_01_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your hound is staring at my hem again, darling. Your Foolishness is offering three to one he chews it.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Barnaby would never savage a lady's wardrobe. Though my own manners are wearing thin tonight.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Nonsense. You still bow like a headliner before every ambush.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: One keeps up the courtesies, if you please. When a gentleman forgets how to bow, the wolf takes over.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then I'll keep calling your cue from the wings until the last curtain.
endif
-> END

~ act3_02_cordelia_silas
if name:cordelia_skein and name:silas_vane and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:cordelia_skein: The wind through your ribs has pitched up a full third since the milepost, Silas. Dread, I'd say.
interject name:silas_vane: A smart player lets the house think his nerve is fraying before he turns the last card.
interject name:cordelia_skein: You've been shuffling those bone slivers at twice your usual pace for an hour.
interject name:silas_vane: When you can see the end of the road, you either keep your hands moving or start counting what you owe.
interject name:cordelia_skein: If my hands tremble at the end, you have my permission to mock me.
endif
-> END

~ act3_03_tobin_silas
if name:tobin_hayward and name:silas_vane and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep that censer downwind, Silas. I'd rather not go up like a beacon before the finish.
interject name:silas_vane: Relax. I banked the herbs an hour ago. And I've been carrying a bucket of ditch water behind you.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You carried a leaky bucket up a mud trail with your knuckles split, and never charged me a copper?
interject name:silas_vane: Don't get misty, you old sack of hay. I need someone standing at the end to tell me my pulse is skipping.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You haven't got a pulse, you daft fraud. Your collar seam's holding up, though.
endif
-> END

~ act3_04_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:rook_coldwake: Your hound is parked on my boot again, Lucan. Three leash statutes.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Forgive him, Rook. He seeks out cold iron when a foul draught comes off the ridge.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Either that, or I dropped a crumb of kettle corn in my boot cuff.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, he has no dignity tonight. Still, it eases my mind to walk beside a shield that never wavers.
interject name:rook_coldwake: The Watch doesn't abandon a post just because the neighbours have poor manners.
endif
-> END

~ act3_05_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Eight sleeves, darling, and not a pucker at the shoulder. I'd pay good money for that pattern.
interject name:cordelia_skein: And your cuff repairs are remarkably neat, Delphine, for stitching done mid-stride with a sail needle.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A girl has to keep her stuffing tucked in, or the critics call the whole act threadbare.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Quite right. Whatever waits at the end of this lane, we'll meet it impeccably tailored.
endif
-> END

~ act3_06_tobin_rook
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:tobin_hayward: You've put that coffin-lid between me and the cinders again, Rook. Didn't even break step.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Embers on a public footway are a hazard, Tobin. Dry straw catches faster than damp bone.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Most watchmen wouldn't think a bundle of twine and field mice worth the trouble.
interject name:rook_coldwake: You walked out of that crash with us. You're on my log, and nobody on my log burns while I can lift a slab.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Then hold still at camp tonight. Your shield strap is fraying right through.
endif
-> END

~ act3_07_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:silas_vane: Ten to one the next ugly thing goes for the lantern first, Lucan. I'll keep asking till you crack.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A gentleman still does not wager on the quarry. Though by this sloppy trail, it's a four at best.
interject name:silas_vane: Four's generous. My own shadow's hugging my heels tighter than your dog.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: "More tightly than your hound does", if you please. Though the dark ahead would rattle anyone's grammar.
interject name:silas_vane: Stick close to my left rib at the door, and we'll see whose manners hold out longer.
endif
-> END

~ act3_08_lucan_rook_tobin
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The air off the Hollow tastes of rust and cellar stone tonight, friends.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Drainage has given out along this stretch, and my knuckles are taking the damp poorly.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Rub your grave-wax in, Rook. And Lucan, stop sniffing the blight like it's vintage cider.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: One must catalogue the night's bouquet, Tobin. Your straw and turnip remain a steady nine.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Keep that lantern clear of his cuffs all the same. One more job before we rest.
endif
-> END

~ act3_09_silas_delphine_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the crone on that moon tonight. Grinning like she holds every marked card and knows our tabs are due.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Let her grin, darling. Your Foolishness has riddles about her, and I intend to spoil her final act.
interject name:cordelia_skein: If you two mean to spit in the moon's eye, keep your voices steady. My notes dissolve if you shout.
interject name:silas_vane: I couldn't ask for better company to strike the match.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: We walk out of this valley together. Even if Cordelia has to stitch us back up by hand.
endif
-> END
